<speak>Separately now. The practical folders are in the cupboard near the desk, and the keepsakes are in a box on a different shelf. I used to mix them because I thought I would remember where each thing was. That works until you are looking for a warranty and find yourself reading old letters instead. I have also written simple labels rather than using abbreviations. Some of my old labels made sense only to me, and even I was beginning to forget them.</speak>